        "date": "2026-03-10T20:49:12Z"
      },
      "message": "Remove execute_unknown from the IDL compiler\n\nexecute_unknown was a post-hoc \"undo\" mechanism on the Executable\ninterface: every assignable node had to implement it to set variables\nto nil (unknown) when traversing conditional branches whose conditions\nare not compile-time-known. It was error-prone (the fadd.s bug showed\nit could be silently bypassed) and semantically wrong for\n\"branch may or may not execute\" cases.\n\nReplacements:\n- Add snapshot_values/restore_values to SymbolTable so IfBodyAst#prune\n  and ForLoopAst#prune can snapshot outer-scope Var values before\n  pruning a body and restore them afterward, then call\n  nullify_assignments to mark loop/branch-assigned vars unknown.\n- Add nullify_assignments overrides to all assignment node types\n  (AryElementAssignmentAst, AryRangeAssignmentAst, FieldAssignmentAst,\n  MultiVariableAssignmentAst, PostIncrementExpressionAst,\n  PostDecrementExpressionAst) so ConditionalStatementAst#execute and\n  IfAst#prune can precisely nullify only the variables a branch would\n  assign, without attempting to execute the branch.\n- Fix AryRangeAssignmentAst#execute to mutate the existing Var directly\n  instead of pushing a shadowing Var via symtab.add, so snapshot/restore\n  correctly undoes the mutation. Also fix the off-by-one in the bit-range\n  mask formula.\n- IfBodyAst#prune gains a restore: parameter; known-true/false branches\n  in IfAst#prune pass restore: false so their assignments persist.\n\nAll execute_unknown implementations and the interface method are deleted.\nRegression tests added for ConditionalStatementAst, ForLoopAst,\nAryRangeAssignmentAst, and AryRangeAssignmentAst#execute value correctness.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "b3ba9ce5c1f8f3786b4f7f8d9b27364edfcdcbce",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-unified-db/git/trees/b3ba9ce5c1f8f3786b4f7f8d9b27364edfcdcbce"
